 * source: corpus/learn/windows-ce-5.0/ms894546(v=msdn.10).html  borrowed from learn
 * row: LINETRANSLATEOPTION_CANCELCALLWAITING = 0x00000002 If a Cancel Call Waiting string is defined for the location, setting this bit will cause that string to be inserted at the beginning of the dialable string. This is commonly used by data modem and fax applications to prevent interruption of calls by call waiting beeps. If no Cancel Call Waiting string is defined for the location, this bit has no affect. Note that applications using this bit are advised to also set the LINECALLPARAMFLAGS_SECURE bit in the dwCallParamFlags member of the LINECALLPARAMS structure passed in to lineMakeCall through the lpCallParams parameter, so that if the line device uses a mechanism other than dialable digits to suppress call interrupts that that mechanism will be invoked. TAPI versions 1.4 and later.
 * source: corpus/learn/windows-ce-net-4x/ms927410(v=msdn.10).html  borrowed from learn
